{"title":"1999 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 3","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><dl><dd><i>The following problem is from the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems\" title=\"1999 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems\">1999 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) #5</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"1999 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems (page does not exist)\">1999 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) #3</a>, so those problems redirect to this page.</i></dd></dl>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Which one of the following gives an odd integer?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/e/a0efbb16c00a3f096bfe96ba406b7c4cf8354d2f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A)}\\ 6^2 \\qquad \\text{(B)}\\ 23-17 \\qquad \\text{(C)}\\ 9\\times 24 \\qquad \\text{(D)}\\ 96\\div 8 \\qquad \\text{(E)}\\ 9\\times 41$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"511\" height=\"21\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Evaluating all of the answer choices, we get:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/2/242bade7eecb8dbe7d1ef62e8008cfb581dbe77d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6^2 = 36$\" width=\"58\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/9/a093f21c8bbc0e04c0a96bbc81234d9d0f0b7044.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$23 - 17 = 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"94\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/5/d25d5d46aa1a04fe168671696a78cea771b1badf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9 \\times 24 = 216$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"103\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/8/a08050344852ed6088196af32d498edcf1d625ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$96 \\div 8 = 12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"94\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/7/35784d7e4b1ee83df48924d7024f51912e53b9f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9 \\times 41 = 369$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"103\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p>The only odd number from the list is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/5/e0506ac4973ff6cdbdab46e1dd4401710162b73b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed {\\textbf{(E) } 9 \\times 41}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"96\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Without evaluating the answers, we can see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/4/e8406a2a50c1aa1040c8862b912a5f3d703d9569.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6^2$\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" /> is the square of an even number, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/3/7135f9ea0908ec3e8b1adc910000ca3442ede584.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9 \\times 24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"15\" /> involves multiplication with an even number, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/6/9c6ce8efbd3f7fa5f4987131355186341dd06bb1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$23 - 17$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"60\" height=\"15\" /> involves two odd numbers, so those are even. This means that we can eliminate those answers.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/8/df8389e66238b9f7af56dab742532f85129cfb15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9 \\times 41$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"15\" /> involves the multiplication of two odd numbers, meaning that it must be the odd number.\n</p><p>Thus, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/5/e0506ac4973ff6cdbdab46e1dd4401710162b73b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed {\\textbf{(E) } 9 \\times 41}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"96\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)\" title=\"1999 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7)\">1999 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7)</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems\" title=\"1999 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"1999 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1999 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1999 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 6